Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 04: THE LAST NORMAL MORNING (CHAPTER 03)

====

EXT. CENTRAL PARK - MORNING

Golden autumn sunlight filters through yellow maple leaves. JOGGERS glide past. Dogs bark. A picture-perfect Manhattan morning.

In the distance, 200 Amsterdam towers like a monument to human invulnerability.

INT. CAFE LUXE - AMSTERDAM & 70TH - CONTINUOUS

An espresso machine HISSES. 

ELENA VANCE (30s, structural investigator) sits at a corner table with her laptop open. She sips her cappuccino.

On her table, a glass of ice water suddenly RIPPLES. 

Not once. A continuous, steady vibration: *one-two-three-four... one-two-three-four.*

Elena stops. She looks down at the glass. 

She pulls out a compact digital seismometer from her bag and places it on the marble cafe table.

The digital readout climbs: `0.02g ... 0.05g ... 0.11g`.

                         ELENA
          (whispering to herself)
          There's no subway line beneath 70th and Amsterdam.

She looks out the window at the 70-story glass tower. 

High above, a flock of SPARROWS suddenly erupts from the tower's cornices, fleeing in panic toward the Hudson.

FADE TO BLACK.
